 fixed by the customer within the Apple Pay sheet, we return an NSError that can be displayed in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise, the original error is returned, resulting in the Apple Pay sheet being dismissed. You should display the error message to the customer afterwards."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Currently, we convert billing address related errors into a PKPaymentError that helpfully points to the billing address field in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Note that Apple Pay should prevent most card errors (e.g. invalid CVC, expired cards) when you add a card to the wallet."}],"url":"\/documentation\/stripeapplepay\/stripecore\/stpapiclient\/pkpaymenterror(forstripeerror:)","title":"pkPaymentError(forStripeError:)"},"doc://com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay/documentation/StripeApplePay/StripeCore":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay\/documentation\/StripeApplePay\/StripeCore","url":"\/documentation\/stripeapplepay\/stripecore","title":"StripeCore"}}}